        "content": "title:\tIssue #1 prototype 0.0.1 — case study + runnable skeleton across every layer\nstate:\tDRAFT\nauthor:\tkonard (Konstantin Diachenko)\nlabels:\t\nassignees:\tkonard (Konstantin Diachenko)\nreviewers:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t2\nurl:\thttps://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/pull/2\nadditions:\t4552\ndeletions:\t125\nauto-merge:\tdisabled\n--\n## Summary\n\nThis PR addresses issue #1 (Personal Meta Profile Sovereign system, prototype 0.0.1) with both:\n\n1. The case study + repository identity (Milestone 0).\n2. A runnable, fully-tested, zero-dependency **skeleton across every architectural layer** of the plan, plus a follow-up iteration that thickens the most user-visible surfaces so the v0.0.1 demo path is reachable end-to-end inside one process.\n\nEach milestone in `docs/case-studies/issue-1/solution-plan.md` is annotated `[skeleton in PR #2]` or `[follow-up]`.\n\nCloses the documentation requirements (R-I1..R-I5) and lands first-pass code for R-A1..R-A5, R-B4, R-C1..R-C5, R-D1..R-D6, R-E1..R-E9 (archive parsing path), R-F1 (web UI), R-F4/R-F5/R-F6 (in-process loopback + vector-clock CRDT), R-F8 (HTTP), R-G1, R-G2 (Rust workspace seed).\n\n## Iteration 2 additions (latest commits)\n\n- **Web UI (`src/web/`)** — vanilla-JS SPA served by the local Node `http` server: chat, contacts, automation graph editor, pattern table with regex inference form, broadcast composer, status. Backed by new `/api/contacts`, `/api/patterns`, `/api/patterns/infer`, `/api/graphs`, `/api/status` routes that derive views from the local store rather than stashing state server-side.\n- **LCS-based regex synthesis + PEG compiler (`src/patterns/`)** — `lcs`-based regex with character-class inference (digit vs. word) for variable gaps, plus `compilePeg` for declarative rules with named captures.\n- **Encrypted backups (`src/storage/backup.js`)** — AES-256-GCM with scrypt KDF; `createBackup` writes `.json.enc` when a passphrase is supplied, `restoreBackup` auto-detects.\n- **Vector-clock CRDT (`src/sync/`)** — `vcInit/vcTick/vcMerge/vcCompare` plus a deterministic concurrent-write tiebreak; Lamport `version` remains the fallback for legacy links.\n- **End-to-end harness (`tests/e2e.test.js`)** — drives the full pipeline over HTTP: import messages, query derived contacts and status, round-trip a backup.\n\n## Quality gates\n\n- `node --test` → **54/54 pass**.\n- `npm run lint` → 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `npm run format:check` → clean.\n- `npm run check:duplication` → clean.\n- `.changeset/issue-1.md` is a single combined entry covering both the skeleton and the iteration-2 additions.\n\n## Runnable skeleton (this PR adds)\n\n| Layer | What lands | Tests |\n| ----- | ---------- | ----- |\n| **Storage** (R-A1..A5, R-F8, R-G1) | `src/storage/`: Universal Links Access, `.lino` codec + `LinoTextStore`, length-prefixed binary `DoubletsStore`, `DualStore` with `verify()`, backup/prune/restore, AES-256-GCM encrypted backups. | `tests/storage.test.js`, `tests/backup.test.js` |\n| **Sources** (R-E1..E9) | `src/sources/`: MessageSource framework + nine adapters (telegram, vk, x, whatsapp, facebook, linkedin, habr-career, hh, superjob); `importInto(store, source, archive)`. | `tests/sources.test.js` |\n| **Patterns** (R-C1, R-C2) | `src/patterns/`: example-driven `inferRegex`, `simplifyRegex`, `matchAll`, LCS-based synthesis with character-class inference, `compilePeg`. | `tests/patterns.test.js` |\n| **Replies** (R-C2) | `src/replies/`: Sørensen-Dice similarity, candidate finder, reply-variation groups, `pickVariation`. | `tests/patterns.test.js` |\n| **Automation** (R-C3, R-C4) | `src/automation/`: tiny graph runtime with pattern → reply → send chains in auto / semi-auto modes. | `tests/automation.test.js` |\n| **CRM + facts** (R-C5, R-D1..D4) | `src/crm/`, `src/facts/`. | `tests/crm.test.js` |\n| **Sync** (R-F5) | `src/sync/`: vector-clock CRDT with Lamport fallback, peer abstraction with echo-suppression, in-process loopback transport. | `tests/sync.test.js` |\n| **Broadcast** (R-B4, R-D5, R-D6) | `src/broadcast/`: cross-network broadcast, profile sync, resume sync. | covered via sources tests |\n| **CLI** (R-A2, R-A4) | `bin/meta-sovereign.js` + `src/cli/`. | `tests/cli.test.js` |\n| **Server** (R-F8) | `src/server/`: Node `http` with `/links`, `/sources`, `/api/contacts`, `/api/patterns`, `/api/patterns/infer`, `/api/graphs`, `/api/status`. | `tests/server.test.js`, `tests/e2e.test.js` |\n| **Web UI** (R-F1) | `src/web/`: vanilla-JS SPA — chat, contacts, automation graphs, patterns, broadcast, status. | covered via `tests/server.test.js` |\n| **Electron** (R-F1, R-F3) | `electron/main.js` opens the local server URL. | manual smoke |\n| **Docker** (R-F6, R-F7) | `docker/web.Dockerfile`, `docker/rtc.Dockerfile`, `docker/docker-compose.yml`. | manual smoke |\n| **Rust port** (R-G2) | `Cargo.toml` workspace + `crates/meta-sovereign-core/`. | `cargo test` |\n\n## Maintainer note\n\nPer the maintainer's directive (\"_implement the full vision as per plan and our original issue_\"), this PR ships a working seed for **every** architectural layer plus a thickening pass on the user-visible surfaces. Remaining milestones (mobile/Electron polish, pure-Rust stack, full WebRTC transport) stay as skeleton stubs and continue milestone-by-milestone per `docs/case-studies/issue-1/solution-plan.md`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` (54/54 pass).\n- [x] `npm run check` (lint + format:check + duplication) clean.\n- [x] CLI smoke: `node bin/meta-sovereign.js sources` prints all 9 networks.\n- [x] Server + SPA smoke covered by `tests/server.test.js`.\n- [x] End-to-end pipeline covered by `tests/e2e.test.js`.\n- [x] Backup round-trip (plain + encrypted) covered by `tests/backup.test.js`.\n- [x] Sync loopback + vector-clock merge covered by `tests/sync.test.js`.\n- [x] All commits on `issue-1-fc41adad29ce`.\n\nRefs: #1\n\nFixes #1",
