        "tool_use_id": "toolu_01NyHsn9wuBGQ2hJtq7w1Dn5",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "Total comments: 18\n\n--- Comment 1 (by konard, at 2026-05-01T09:00:14Z) ---\n## Working session summary\n\nAll checks green:\n- Title: \"Case study and repository identity for issue #1 (Prototype 0.0.1)\"\n- isDraft: false, mergeable: MERGEABLE, state: OPEN\n- All non-skipped checks: SUCCESS (Broken Link Checker, Manual Version Check, Detect Changes, Lint and Format, Validate Documentation, all 9 Test matrix jobs across node/bun/deno × ubuntu/macos/windows)\n\nPR #2 is ready for review: https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/pull/2\n\nSummary of work landed:\n- **Repository identity**: package renamed from template `my-package` → `meta-sovereign`; description, keywords, repo URL, and changeset script `PACKAGE_NAME` constants updated; README and CONTRIBUTING reflect the new project.\n- **Case study** in `docs/case-studies/issue-1/`: README, `requirements.md` (35 atomic IDs R-A1..R-I5), `components.md` (every issue-linked repo), `external-research.md` (local-first, CRDTs, Beeper/Matrix, regex synthesis, fuzzy search, node editors, WebRTC, encryption, browser SQLite, cross-platform shells), `architecture.md` (Universal Links Access API, MessageSource interface, dual-stack), `solution-plan.md` (14 phased milestones with definition of done for v0.0.1), and `data/` raw issue JSON.\n- **Changeset**: `.changeset/case-study-issue-1.md` describing the minor bump.\n- All CI green; format, lint, tests pass on every OS × runtime combo.\n\n---\n*This summary was automatically extracted from the AI working session output.*\n\n--- Comment 2 (by konard, at 2026-05-01T09:00:25Z) ---\n## 🤖 Solution Draft Log\nThis log file contains the complete execution trace of the AI solution draft process.\n\n### 💰 Cost: **$6.291001**\n\n### 📊 **Context and tokens usage:**\n\n**Claude Opus 4.7:** (2 session segments)\n1. peak request: 24.0K / 1M (2%) input tokens, 39.0K / 128K (30%) output tokens\n2. peak request: 30.5K / 1M (3%) input tokens, 7.7K / 128K (6%) outpu