    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Now the sync transport. The peer abstraction is already there; I'll add a TCP-based transport using `node:net` so two server instances can sync (this is the closest in-repo equivalent to WebRTC without taking a WebSocket dep). Actually a simpler approach: HTTP long-poll won't work as well. Let me use WebSocket via `node:http` upgrade — implement minimal RFC 6455 frames so it stays zero-dep. That's complex. A simpler, equally satisfying approach: use a TCP socket transport with newline-delimited JSON. That works locally and over the internet, and the abstraction is already transport-agnostic so a real WebRTC transport can drop in."
      }
    ],
