        "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user invoked the AI to continue working on PR #2 of `link-foundation/meta-sovereign` (issue #1: \"Prototype version 0.0.1\" — a personal meta profile sovereign system). The session opened with `Continue.` after notifying that 4 new PR comments existed and the PR description had been edited. Reading the PR comments revealed the maintainer's explicit and repeated directive: implement the **full vision** of issue #1 in this single PR, do not punt anything to follow-up PRs, \"every feature should be usable, and you should predict required human interface so everything is consistent and works perfectly.\" Two prior iterations had already landed: (1) skeleton across every architectural layer, (2) thickening of user-visible surfaces (web SPA, LCS regex synthesis, encrypted backups, vector-clock CRDT, e2e test). My job in this session is **iteration 3** — push deeper toward fully-implemented features and a complete UI surface.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Local-first/sovereign architecture — Universal Links Access API\n   - DualStore = LinoTextStore (text) + DoubletsStore (binary), with `verify()`\n   - `links-notation` indented format (R-A5)\n   - MessageSource adapter framework (9 networks: telegram, vk, x, whatsapp, facebook, linkedin, habr-career, hh, superjob)\n   - Vector-clock CRDT with Lamport fallback + deterministic concurrent-write tiebreak\n   - Pattern matching: `inferRegex` (column-aligned) + `inferRegexLcs` (LCS skeleton with character-class inference) + `compilePeg` (named captures)\n   - Reply variation groups + Sørensen-Dice fuzzy candidate finder\n   - Automation graph: pattern → reply → send/wait nodes, auto / semi-auto modes\n   - Set-algebra audience query language (AND/OR/NOT, dimensions: network/chat/sender/kind/fact)\n   - Zero-runtime-dep philosophy — Node built-ins only (`http`, `net`, `crypto`)\n   - Test framework: `test-anywhere` with describe/it/expect\n   - eslint complexity budget: 15\n   - PR uses jscpd, prettier, eslint quality gates\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - `docs/case-studies/issue-1/solution-plan.md` (read fully)\n     - Source of truth for milestones; iteration 3 must cover gaps and update the \"[skeleton in PR #2]\" annotations to \"done\" where appropriate.\n   - `docs/case-studies/issue-1/requirements.md` (read fully)\n     - 35 atomic requirement IDs (R-A1..R-I5) — used to plan iteration 3 deliverables.\n   - `src/index.js` (read) — lists all sub-namespaces exported.\n   - `src/server/index.js` (rewritten)\n     - Old version had ~250 lines with many inline route handlers. Rewrote as thin router that delegates to route modules to stay below complexity 15. Includes static asset serving for SPA shell + js/css/svg.\n   - `src/server/util.js` (NEW)\n     - Shared `json`, `text`, `readBody` helpers.\n   - `src/server/routes-derived.js` (NEW)\n     - Read-only routes: `/api/contacts`, `/api/status`, `/api/autocomplete`, `/api/audience`, `/api/facts`, `/api/search`. Includes the audience expression parser supporting `AND/OR/NOT/()` over `network:`/`chat:`/`sender:`/`kind:`/`fact:` tokens.\n   - `src/server/routes-mutating.js` (NEW)\n     - CRUD routes: `/links`, `/api/patterns` (GET/PUT/infer), `/api/graphs` (GET/PUT/run), `/api/replies` (GET/PUT), `/api/profile` (GET/PUT), `/api/resume` (GET/PUT), `/api/broadcast` (POST). Includes `hydrateGraph` that converts persisted regex strings back to RegExp before running.\n   - `src/web/index.html` (updated) — nav now lists: Chat, Operator, Contacts, Automation, Patterns, Replies, Facts, Audience, Broadcast, Profile, Status.\n   - `src/web/dom.js` (NEW)\n     - `h(tag, attrs, children)` DOM helper + `api` object with all REST endpoints (autocomplete, audience, facts, profile, resume, replies, etc.).\n   - `src/web/views.js` (NEW, large file)\n     - 11 view renderers: `chatView` (with autocomplete-on-type and message composer that PUTs back), `operatorView` (DONE/NEXT card stream with D/N keyboard hotkeys, R-B3), `contactsView` (with last-seen + chat counts), `automationView`, `patternsView` (with inference mode toggle simple/lcs and persistence), `repliesView` (group editor with variations), `factsView` (per-answerer Q→A tables), `audienceView` (set-algebra query input + result), `broadcastView`, `profileView` (profile + resume editors with planned syncs), `statusView`.\n   - `src/web/app.js` (rewritten) — thin module that imports all views and switches on nav clicks.\n   - `src/web/app.css` (rewritten) — expanded styles for new components (composer, completions chips, operator card, profile forms, audience output).\n   - `src/sync/tcp-transport.js` (NEW)\n     ```js\n     // newline-delimited JSON over TCP, plugs into createPeer's transport contract\n     export const startSyncListener = ({ port = 0 } = {}) => Promise<{port, transport, close}>\n     export const connectSyncPeer = ({ port, host = '127.0.0.1' } = {}) => Promise<{transport, close}>\n     ```\n   - `src/sync/index.js` (modified) — re-exports `startSyncListener`, `connectSyncPeer`.\n   - `tests/sync-tcp.test.js` (NEW) — verifies a `put` on store A replicates to store B over TCP through `createPeer.connect(transport)`. Already passing (55/55).\n   - `tests/server-iter3.test.js` (NEW) — exercises every new endpoint (patterns persist, replies persist, graph save+run, facts, autocomplete, audience, search, profile/resume sync planning, broadcast, status). **NOT YET RUN** — about to execute `npm test` to verify.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `npm test` initially failed with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND: 'test-anywhere'` because dependencies were not installed in the fresh worktree. Fixed by running `npm install`.\n   - User feedback in earlier PR comments: the initial PR scoped itself to \"out of scope: importer adapters, UI, Web