in this pull request fully. Please plan and execute everything in a single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context autocompacts and you can continue indefinetely, do as much as possible in one go, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\"\n     - \"Please continue to execute on full vision, I don't care about your opinions and evaluations, you have unlimited time, and this pull request still don't have enough changes to slow down the GitHub UI, keep going, implement the full vision as per plan and our original issue. It will not take years if you will just silently work until it done.\"\n     - \"Please continue to execute on full vision until it is fully done in this pull request. Read the existing plan, make sure done things are totally done and marked as done. Double check it fully implements the vision of https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/issues/1. All features should be usable, and you should predict required human interface, so everything consistent and works perfectly.\"\n   - System reminders about deferred tools, available skills (update-config, schedule, etc.), task tool usage.\n   - The final assistant turn ended with creation of `tests/server-iter3.test.js`; the next user-side message was the summary request itself.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - #2 Mark/verify completed milestones in solution-plan.md (update annotations from \"[skeleton in PR #2]\" to \"[done in PR #2]\" where iteration 3 closes them; add iteration 3 section).\n   - #6 finish — sync transport (TCP done; document in plan).\n   - #7 Thicken Rust core (`crates/meta-sovereign-core`) — port lino tokenizer + LinoTextStore reading; document parity with JS.\n   - #8 lino-arguments-style CLI — extend `bin/meta-sovereign.js` + `src/cli/index.js` with `audience`, `extract-facts`, `serve-rtc`, `sync-connect`, `broadcast` subcommands.\n   - #9 TypeDoc / JSDoc generation — add npm script + config; produce `docs/api/`.\n