        "content": "1\t//! `meta-sovereign-core` — Rust counterpart of `src/storage` (R-G2).\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Today the crate exposes the [`Link`] type and a `MemoryStore` so\n4\t//! the workspace compiles green. Subsequent PRs add the LinoTextStore\n5\t//! and DoubletsStore (via `doublets-rs`) that mirror the JS API\n6\t//! one-to-one, so a Rust-only deployment of the server remains\n7\t//! feature-complete with the JS one.\n8\t\n9\tuse std::collections::HashMap;\n10\t\n11\t#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n12\tpub struct Link {\n13\t    pub id: String,\n14\t    pub tokens: Vec<String>,\n15\t    pub children: Vec<String>,\n16\t}\n17\t\n18\t#[derive(Default)]\n19\tpub struct MemoryStore {\n20\t    data: HashMap<String, Link>,\n21\t}\n22\t\n23\timpl MemoryStore {\n24\t    pub fn new() -> Self {\n25\t        Self::default()\n26\t    }\n27\t    pub fn put(&mut self, link: Link) {\n28\t        self.data.insert(link.id.clone(), link);\n29\t    }\n30\t    pub fn get(&self, id: &str) -> Option<&Link> {\n31\t        self.data.get(id)\n32\t    }\n33\t    pub fn delete(&mut self, id: &str) -> bool {\n34\t        self.data.remove(id).is_some()\n35\t    }\n36\t    pub fn query(&self) -> Vec<&Link> {\n37\t        self.data.values().collect()\n38\t    }\n39\t}\n40\t\n41\t#[cfg(test)]\n42\tmod tests {\n43\t    use super::*;\n44\t    #[test]\n45\t    fn round_trip() {\n46\t        let mut s = MemoryStore::new();\n47\t        let l = Link {\n48\t            id: \"a\".into(),\n49\t            tokens: vec![\"hello\".into()],\n50\t            children: vec![],\n51\t        };\n52\t        s.put(l.clone());\n53\t        assert_eq!(s.get(\"a\"), Some(&l));\n54\t        assert!(s.delete(\"a\"));\n55\t        assert_eq!(s.query().len(), 0);\n56\t    }\n57\t}\n58\t"
