        "text": "Found it: `json()` returns `undefined`. So `json(res, 200, x) ?? true` → `true`. That's correct.\n\nBut `handlePrefixedGet` and `handlePrefixedPut` return `json(res, ...)` directly (not wrapped in `?? true`). They return `undefined`. Then `handlePatterns` does `return handlePrefixedGet(store, res, 'pattern') ?? true` — since `handlePrefixedGet` is async, that returns a Promise that resolves to `undefined`, and `Promise ?? true` → the Promise truthy → returns `true`. That looks ok actually...\n\nWait, the issue: `handlePatterns` is async but doesn't `await` `handlePrefixedGet`. So `handlePrefixedGet(...)` returns a Promise (truthy), `Promise ?? true` → Promise. Then the outer `await handlePatterns(...)` resolves to that returned-but-not-awaited Promise's resolved value... actually `await` on a Promise that resolves to a Promise will chain. So it eventually resolves to `undefined ?? true` — but wait, that nullish-coalesce happens BEFORE the await. So `handlePatterns` returns `await ... return Promise` which resolves to undefined (from the unawaited handler). So `handleMutatingRoutes` sees `undefined` from `handlePatterns`, falls through, tries `handleDerivedRoutes`, which also doesn't match, falls through to `json(res, 404, ...)`. But by then the inner handler has already written! That's the double-write.\n\nThe fix: `await` the helper call before applying `?? true`."
