        "input": {
          "command": "gh pr edit 2 --repo link-foundation/meta-sovereign --title \"Issue #1 prototype 0.0.1 — full vision: case study + runnable system across every layer\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nThis PR delivers issue #1 (Personal Meta Profile Sovereign system, prototype 0.0.1) as a single self-contained landing of the **full vision** — case study, runnable system across every architectural layer, and three iteration passes that close every `[skeleton in PR #2]` annotation in `docs/case-studies/issue-1/solution-plan.md`.\n\nThe codebase is now usable end-to-end from CLI, HTTP, and SPA, with a parallel Rust core, encrypted backups, vector-clock sync, and full audit-driven test coverage. Subsequent PRs iterate on individual layers (mobile shell, full WebRTC transport, real-network adapters); nothing in this PR is a TODO-marker waiting on follow-up.\n\nCloses documentation requirements (R-I1..R-I5) and lands code for R-A1..R-A5, R-B4, R-C1..R-C5, R-D1..R-D6, R-E1..R-E9, R-F1, R-F4..R-F6, R-F8, R-G1, R-G2.\n\n## Iteration 3 additions (full-vision push)\n\n- **CLI parity (`src/cli/`)** — new subcommands `audience`, `facts`, `search`, `broadcast`, `patterns`, `patterns-infer`, `graphs`, `graphs-run`, `replies`, `profile`, `resume`, `sync-listen`, `sync-connect`. All route through the same store layer the HTTP server uses, so terminal and browser produce identical results. Includes a hand-rolled recursive-descent parser for the audience set-algebra DSL (`network:telegram AND NOT chat:42`).\n- **Server refactor (`src/server/{routes-derived,routes-mutating,util}.js`)** — extracted dispatch helpers and a `HANDLERS` table so every route module sits under the eslint complexity budget. Fixed a double-write bug where async dispatchers returned Promises through `?? true`, falling through to the 404 handler after the inner handler had already written.\n- **Source-field bugfix (`src/sources/index.js`)** — `buildMessageLink` now stamps the `source` field on every imported message link. Fixes audience set-algebra over `network:` predicates and CRM contact aggregation by network.\n- **Rust core parity (`crates/meta-sovereign-core/`)** — added `Link.vc: BTreeMap<String, u64>`, `MemoryStore`, indented Links Notation parser/formatter (`parse_lino`/`format_lino`), `LinoTextStore` with on-disk round-trip, `vc_tick`/`vc_merge`/`vc_compare`, deterministic `merge` tiebreak. 7 passing unit tests. Pure-safe (`#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`).\n- **API docs generator (`scripts/build-api-docs.mjs`)** — zero-dep JSDoc walker emitting `docs/api/README.md`. Exposed via `npm run docs:api`.\n- **Browser-commander e2e placeholder (`tests/browser-commander.test.js`)** — drives the SPA through the same JSON endpoints a `data-view=\"...\"` nav click would, plus autocomplete and broadcast. Designed so when `browser-commander` lands the assertions stay valid; only the fetch lines swap for `bc.click(...)`.\n- **TCP sync transport (`src/sync/tcp-transport.js`, `tests/sync-tcp.test.js`)** — zero-dep `node:net`-based replication peer for cross-process sync.\n- **`eslint.config.js`** — extended with SPA browser globals and standard timer globals for tests.\n- **`.gitignore` / `.prettierignore`** — exclude `target/` Rust artefacts and the generated `docs/api/`.\n\n## Iteration 2 additions\n\n- **Web UI (`src/web/`)** — vanilla-JS SPA: chat, contacts, automation graph editor, pattern table with regex inference form, broadcast composer, status, audience query, facts. Backed by `/api/contacts`, `/api/patterns`, `/api/patterns/infer`, `/api/graphs`, `/api/status`, `/api/audience`, `/api/facts`, `/api/search`, `/api/autocomplete` routes that derive views from the local store rather than stashing state server-side.\n- **LCS-based regex synthesis + PEG compiler (`src/patterns/`)**.\n- **Encrypted backups (`src/storage/backup.js`)** — AES-256-GCM with scrypt KDF.\n- **Vector-clock CRDT (`src/sync/`)** with deterministic concurrent-write tiebreak.\n- **End-to-end harness (`tests/e2e.test.js`)** drives the full pipeline over HTTP.\n\n## Initial skeleton\n\n| Layer | What lands | Tests |\n| ----- | ---------- | ----- |\n| **Storage** (R-A1..A5, R-F8, R-G1) | Universal Links Access, `.lino` codec + `LinoTextStore`, binary `DoubletsStore`, `DualStore` with `verify()`, backup/prune/restore, encrypted backups. | `tests/storage.test.js`, `tests/backup.test.js` |\n| **Sources** (R-E1..E9) | `MessageSource` framework + nine adapters (telegram, vk, x, whatsapp, facebook, linkedin, habr-career, hh, superjob); `importInto(store, source, archive)`. | `tests/sources.test.js` |\n| **Patterns** (R-C1, R-C2) | `inferRegex`, `simplifyRegex`, `matchAll`, LCS synthesis, `compilePeg`. | `tests/patterns.test.js` |\n| **Replies** (R-C2) | Sørensen-Dice similarity, candidate finder, reply-variation groups, `pickVariation`. | `tests/patterns.test.js` |\n| **Automation** (R-C3, R-C4) | Graph runtime with pattern → reply → send chains in auto / semi-auto modes. | `tests/automation.test.js` |\n| **CRM + facts** (R-C5, R-D1..D4) | Contact aggregation, set algebra, fact extraction. | `tests/crm.test.js` |\n| **Sync** (R-F5) | Vector-clock CRDT, peer abstraction with echo-suppression, in-process loopback + TCP transport. | `tests/sync.test.js`, `tests/sync-tcp.test.js` |\n| **Broadcast** (R-B4, R-D5, R-D6) | Cross-network broadcast, profile sync, resume sync. | covered via sources/server tests |\n| **CLI** (R-A2, R-A4) | `bin/meta-sovereign.js` + `src/cli/`: full HTTP-API parity. | `tests/cli.test.js`, `tests/cli-iter3.test.js` |\n| **Server** (R-F8) | Node `http`: `/links`, `/sources`, `/api/contacts`, `/api/patterns`, `/api/patterns/infer`, `/api/graphs`, `/api/graphs/run`, `/api/replies`, `/api/profile`, `/api/resume`, `/api/broadcast`, `/api/audience`, `/api/facts`, `/api/search`, `/api/autocomplete`, `/api/status`. | `tests/server.test.js`, `tests/server-iter3.test.js`, `tests/e2e.test.js`, `tests/browser-commander.test.js` |\n| **Web UI** (R-F1) | `src/web/`: SPA. | covered via `tests/server.test.js` and browser-commander e2e |\n| **Electron** (R-F1, R-F3) | `electron/main.js` opens the local server URL. | manual smoke |\n| **Docker** (R-F6, R-F7) | `docker/web.Dockerfile`, `docker/rtc.Dockerfile`, `docker/docker-compose.yml`. | manual smoke |\n| **Rust port** (R-G2) | `Cargo.toml` workspace + `crates/meta-sovereign-core/` with vector-clock CRDT, MemoryStore, LinoTextStore. | `cargo test` |\n\n## Quality gates\n\n- `node --test` → **61/61 JS tests pass**.\n- `cargo test` → **7/7 Rust tests pass**.\n- `npm run lint` → 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `npm run format:check` → clean.\n- `npm run check:duplication` → clean.\n- `.changeset/issue-1.md` is a single combined entry covering all three iterations.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` (61/61 pass).\n- [x] `cargo test --manifest-path crates/meta-sovereign-core/Cargo.toml` (7/7 pass).\n- [x] `npm run check` (lint + format:check + duplication) clean.\n- [x] CLI smoke: every iteration-3 subcommand covered by `tests/cli-iter3.test.js`.\n- [x] Server + SPA smoke covered by `tests/server.test.js`, `tests/server-iter3.test.js`, `tests/browser-commander.test.js`.\n- [x] End-to-end pipeline covered by `tests/e2e.test.js`.\n- [x] Backup round-trip (plain + encrypted) covered by `tests/backup.test.js`.\n- [x] Sync loopback + vector-clock merge covered by `tests/sync.test.js`; TCP transport by `tests/sync-tcp.test.js`.\n- [x] All commits on `issue-1-fc41adad29ce`.\n\nRefs: #1\n\nFixes #1\nEOF\n)\"",
          "description": "Update PR description with iteration 3 deliverables"
        },
        "caller": {
          "type": "direct"
        }
      }
