      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (maintainer konard, deep.assistant.team@proton.me) directed via PR #2 comments that this single PR must implement the **full vision** of issue #1 (Personal Meta Profile Sovereign system, prototype 0.0.1) — closing every `[skeleton in PR #2]` annotation in `docs/case-studies/issue-1/solution-plan.md`, delivering a complete UI surface, full CLI parity, Rust core parity, API docs, and a browser-commander e2e placeholder. Quote: \"_All features should be usable, and you should predict required human interface, so everything consistent and works perfectly._\" This session resumed iteration 3 work and pushed it through CI to a green state. The session-final user message was a non-functional instruction: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — i.e. produce this summary.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Local-first/sovereign architecture, Universal Links Access API\n   - DualStore = LinoTextStore + DoubletsStore + verify()\n   - `links-notation` indented format\n   - Vector-clock CRDT with deterministic concurrent-write tiebreak (`vcInit/vcTick/vcMerge/vcCompare`)\n   - Pattern matching: `inferRegex`, `inferRegexLcs`, `simplifyRegex`, `compilePeg`\n   - Reply variation groups + Sørensen-Dice fuzzy finder\n   - Automation graph (pattern→reply→send/wait), auto/semi-auto modes\n   - Set-algebra audience query language (AND/OR/NOT) over `network:`/`chat:`/`sender:`/`kind:`/`fact:`\n   - Zero-runtime-dep philosophy — Node built-ins only (`http`, `net`, `crypto`)\n   - Test framework: `test-anywhere` with describe/it/expect — runs under Node, Bun, and Deno\n   - Bun default `it()` timeout = 5000 ms\n   - Deno test runtime uses fetch-response-body leak detection\n   - eslint complexity budget: 15 (warn only)\n   - jscpd, prettier, eslint quality gates\n   - Rust crate uses `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`\n   - `gh` CLI for PR management; `gh pr ready 2` to lift draft\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - `src/server/routes-mutating.js`\n     - Deleted dead `_unusedRepliesEnd` function (lines 125-137) left over from a sloppy prior edit.\n     - Fixed the async/Promise dispatch bug. Helpers now write the response then `return true` directly; dispatchers `return helperCall()` without `?? true`. Without this fix, an unawaited Promise resolved to `undefined`, causing the outer chain to fall through to a 404 handler that double-wrote the response (`ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT` at src/server/index.js:120). Final shape:\n       ```js\n       const handlePrefixedPut = async (store, req, res, prefix, kind) => {\n         const link = await readBody(req);\n         if (!link.id?.startsWith(`${prefix}:`)) {\n           json(res, 400, { error: `${kind}.id must start with \"${prefix}:\"` });\n           return true;\n         }\n         await store.put(link);\n         json(res, 200, link);\n         return true;\n       };\n       const handlePatterns = async (store, req, res, p) => {\n         if (p === '/api/patterns' && req.method === 'GET') {\n           return handlePrefixedGet(store, res, 'pattern');\n         }\n         if (p === '/api/patterns' && req.method === 'PUT') {\n           return handlePrefixedPut(store, req, res, 'pattern', 'pattern');\n         }\n         if (p === '/api/patterns/infer' && req.method === 'POST') {\n           return handlePatternInfer(req, res);\n         }\n         return false;\n       };\n       ```\n     - Same shape applied to `handleGraphs`, `handleGraphRun`, `handlePatternInfer`, `handleReplies`, `handlePrefixedGet`.\n\n   - `src/server/routes-derived.js` (verified correct)\n     - Line 207: `return json(res, 200, await handler(store, url)) ?? true;` — `await` is on `handler()`, `json()` is sync returning undefined, `undefined ?? true` is `true`. Correct.\n\n   - `.prettierignore` (modified)\n     - Added `target` and `docs/api/`:\n       ```\n       node_modules\n       coverage\n       dist\n       target\n       *.min.js\n       package-lock.json\n       .eslintcache\n       CLAUDE.md\n       # Generated API docs (built by scripts/build-api-docs.mjs).\n       docs/api/\n       # Case study raw data files (downloaded from external sources)\n       docs/case-studies/*/data/\n       ```\n\n   - `.gitignore` (modified)\n     - Appended:\n       ```\n       # Rust workspace build artefacts\n       target/\n       # Generated API docs (rebuilt by `npm run docs:api`)\n       docs/api/\n       ```\n\n   - `.changeset/issue-1.md` (modified)\n     - Replaced \"Tests: 54/54 pass …\" trailer with iteration 3 deliverables — CLI parity, server refactor (helpers + dispatch table + double-write fix), `buildMessageLink.source` bugfix, Rust core parity, API docs generator, browser-commander e2e, TCP sync transport, eslint and prettier ignore extensions. New trailer: `Tests: 61/61 JS + 7/7 Rust pass. Lint: 0 errors. Format: clean. Duplication: clean.`\n\n   - `tests/browser-commander.test.js` (modified — first CI fix)\n     - Added body consumption for `/app.js` and `/app.css` to silence Deno's leak detector:\n       ```js\n       const appJs = await fetch(`${base}/app.js`);\n       expect(appJs.status).toBe(200);\n       await appJs.text();\n       const appCss = await fetch(`${base}/app.css`);\n       expect(appCss.status).toBe(200);\n       await appCss.text();\n       ```\n\n   - `tests/sync-tcp.test.js` (modified twice)\n     - First fix replaced `setTimeout(r, 80)` sleep with a 5-second polling deadline. Failed on bun-macOS because polling deadline = bun default test timeout, so test framework killed it at exactly 5002 ms.\n     - Second fix (uncommitted at summary time) uses a deterministic subscribe-based signal:\n       ```js\n       const replicatedSignal = new Promise((resolve) => {\n         const off = b.subscribe((event) => {\n           if (event.type === 'put' && event.link.id === 'x') {\n             off();\n             resolve(event.link);\n           }\n         });\n       });\n       await a.put({ id: 'x', tokens: ['hello'], vc: { a: 1 } });\n       const replicated = await replicatedSignal;\n       expect(replicated?.tokens?.[0]).toBe('hello');\n       ```\n\n   - `src/sync/tcp-transport.js` (read but not edited)\n     - Newline-delimited JSON over TCP. `wireRead` accumulates `chunk.toString('utf8')` and parses lines. `wireSend(socket, event)` writes `JSON.stringify(event) + '\\n'`. `startSyncListener` accepts and tracks all sockets; `connectSyncPeer` connects with a single socket.\n\n   - `src/sync/index.js` (read)\n     - Vector-clock primitives, `merge` with deterministic tiebreak, `createPeer(store, { node })` with `subscribe`-based local fan-out and `receive` mute flag, `loopback()`, and re-exports `startSyncListener/connectSyncPeer` from tcp-transport.\n\n   - `src/storage/universal.js` (read)\n     - `createMemoryStore` is a Map-backed store emitting `{ type: 'put' | 'delete', link }` events on `subscribe(handler)`. The subscribe API is what enabled the deterministic test signal.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n\n   - **Three local test failures: `ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT` at src/server/index.js:120**\n     - Root cause: helpers like `handlePrefixedGet` returned `json(res,...)` which returns `undefined`. Dispatchers wrote `return helperCall(...) ?? true`. Since `helperCall` is async, this evaluated `Promise ?? true` (Promise is truthy, returns Promise), but the outer caller then `await`s the dispatcher, which awaits the unawaited Promise to `undefined`. The dispatch chain saw `undefined`, treated it as falsy, and fell through to the 404 handler — double-writing.\n     - Fix: helpers explicitly `return true` after writing; dispatchers `return helperCall()` without `?? true`.\n\n   - **Prettier flagged docs/api/README.md, solution-plan.md, target/ artefacts**\n     - Fixed by adding `target` and `docs/api/` to `.prettierignore`, and formatting solution-plan.md with `npx prettier --write docs/case-studies/issue-1/solution-plan.md`.\n\n   - **CI (after first push, commit 0793687): Deno on all 3 OSes failed with \"Leaks detected: A fetch response body was created during the test, but not consumed\" at tests/browser-commander.test.js:50**\n     - Root cause: lines 76-77 used `expect((await fetch(...)).status).toBe(200)` without consuming the body.\n     - Fix: capture the response, assert status, then `await response.text()`.\n\n   - **CI (after first push): Bun on macOS failed `Expected undefined to be \"hello\"` at tests/sync-tcp.test.js:32**\n     - Root cause: 80 ms `setTimeout` race; bun-macOS occasionally needs longer than 80 ms for TCP roundtrip + receive() to settle.\n     - First fix attempt: poll loop with 5-second deadline. Failed because bun's default test timeout is exactly 5000 ms — test was killed at 5002 ms before poll completed.\n     - Second fix (uncommitted): subscribe-based deterministic signal using `b.subscribe(...)` to resolve a Promise when the put event arrives at store B.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Diagnosed and fixed a real concurrency bug in routes-mutating.js (double-response writes) that was masked by the dispatcher's truthy Promise.\n   - Cleaned up prettier scope (Rust target/, generated docs) so format:check is sustainable.\n   - Iteratively chased two CI flakes: Deno leak detector and bun-macOS test timeout. The first is fully fixed and verified. The second has one failed attempt (poll loop tied to bun's test-timeout deadline) and one untested fix (subscribe signal).\n   - Local verification: Node 61/61 ✓, Deno 61/61 ✓ (full suite), bun-Linux 2/2 ✓ on the changed tests.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The opening resume directive (covered in the carried-forward summary): \"Please continue to execute on full vision until it is fully done in this pull request. Read the existing plan, make sure done things are totally done and marked as done. Double check it fully implements the vision of https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/issues/1. All features should be usable, and you should predict required human interface, so everything consistent and works perfectly.\"\n   - \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools. ... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far ...\" — instruction triggering this summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Verify the new subscribe-based `tests/sync-tcp.test.js` passes locally on Node, Deno, and bun.\n   - Commit + push the second sync-tcp fix to branch `issue-1-fc41adad29ce`.\n   - Watch the resulting CI run; confirm bun-macOS now passes (and that no new regressions appear).\n   - If bun-macOS still fails, escalate the diagnosis: inspect whether `socket.write` is actually flushing, whether `chunk.toString('utf8')` works on bun-macOS (may need `Buffer.from(chunk).toString('utf8')`), or add a TCP-level acknowledgement.\n   - Final PR description + `gh pr ready 2` are already done from earlier in the session.\n   - Iteration 3 task #11 (\"Update PR description + run full local quality gates\") remains in_progress until CI is fully green on the new SHA.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before the summary request, I was fixing the bun-macOS CI failure for the second time. The first fix (replacing fixed sleep with a 5-second poll loop) had failed because bun's default `it()` test timeout is exactly 5000 ms, equal to my polling deadline — bun killed the test at 5002 ms before the poll could see the replication. I edited `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1777634738460/tests/sync-tcp.test.js` to use a subscribe-based deterministic signal:\n\n   ```js\n   describe('sync over TCP transport', () => {\n     it('replicates a put from one store to another', async () => {\n       const a = createMemoryStore();\n       const b = createMemoryStore();\n       const peerA = createPeer(a, { node: 'a' });\n       const peerB = createPeer(b, { node: 'b' });\n\n       const listener = await startSyncListener({ port: 0 });\n       const offA = peerA.connect(listener.transport);\n\n       const client = await connectSyncPeer({ port: listener.port });\n       const offB = peerB.connect(client.transport);\n\n       // Subscribe to store B before the put so we get a deterministic\n       // signal when replication arrives — avoids a race against bun's\n       // 5-second test timeout on slower CI runners (notably macOS).\n       const replicatedSignal = new Promise((resolve) => {\n         const off = b.subscribe((event) => {\n           if (event.type === 'put' && event.link.id === 'x') {\n             off();\n             resolve(event.link);\n           }\n         });\n       });\n\n       await a.put({\n         id: 'x',\n         tokens: ['hello'],\n         vc: { a: 1 },\n       });\n\n       const replicated = await replicatedSignal;\n       expect(replicated?.tokens?.[0]).toBe('hello');\n\n       offA();\n       offB();\n       await client.close();\n       await listener.close();\n     });\n   });\n   ```\n\n   This edit is saved on disk but NOT yet committed or pushed. I had just inspected `node_modules/test-anywhere/src/index.js` to confirm timeout support patterns and was about to verify the new test locally before committing.\n\n   Branch: `issue-1-fc41adad29ce`. Latest pushed commit: `374af3a \"Fix flaky CI on Deno + bun-macOS\"`. CI run for that SHA: `25213264339` — Test (bun on macos-latest) is the only remaining failure; all others pass.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Run the new subscribe-based test under all three runtimes to verify (`npm test`, `deno test --allow-read --allow-write --allow-env --allow-net --allow-sys tests/sync-tcp.test.js`, `bun test tests/sync-tcp.test.js`), then commit with a message referencing the bun-macOS deadline race (\"Use subscribe signal instead of poll loop in sync-tcp test — bun's 5s default it() timeout was equal to the poll deadline\"), push to `issue-1-fc41adad29ce`, then poll the resulting CI run with `gh run list --branch issue-1-fc41adad29ce --limit 3` and confirm Test (bun on macos-latest) passes. From the most recent context: \"I edited tests/sync-tcp.test.js to use the subscribe signal. ... This was just edited but not yet committed/tested when the user requested the summary.\" If, after push, bun-macOS still times out, the next escalation is to suspect that bun-macOS isn't actually delivering the TCP `data` event for some reason and to add `Buffer.from(chunk).toString('utf8')` defensive handling in `src/sync/tcp-transport.js`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1777634738460/0c89fd5d-c745-4dfb-a135-866319a19411.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."
