nt":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/issues/comments/4358648347","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/pull/2#issuecomment-4358648347","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/issues/2","id":4358648347,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSRd4l88AAAABA8uyGw","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-01T09:13:10Z","updated_at":"2026-05-01T09:13:10Z","body":"## Re-opening scope per maintainer feedback\n\nAcknowledged. The previous PR scoped itself to documentation + repo identity; you've asked for *all* requirements (R-A1..R-I5) implemented in this single PR.\n\n### Honest framing\n\nThe issue describes a multi-year product (unified messenger across 9 networks, operator UI, n8n-style automation graph, regex/PEG synthesis, CRDT/WebRTC sync, Electron+CLI+Docker+web, parallel pure-Rust port, full HIG-grade UI, e2e via browser-commander). I cannot ship a polished v1 of all of that in one session. What I *can* do in one session is land a coherent **runnable skeleton for every subsystem** — minimal but real code, with passing unit tests, so future PRs become feature-by-feature thickening rather than greenfield work.\n\n### Plan for this PR (in addition to existing case study)\n\n1. **Storage** — `UniversalLinksAccess` interface + `LinoTextStore` (indented links-notation reader/writer) + `DoubletsStore` adapter shim + `DualStore` write-through. Round-trip tests. (R-A2/A3/A5/F8/G1)\n2. **Backups + .lino import/export** — snapshot helper + retention math + CLI subcommands. (R-A1/A4)\n3. **`MessageSource` framework + 9 adapter stubs** — Telegram, VK, X, WhatsApp, Facebook, LinkedIn, career.habr.com, hh.ru, superjob.ru. Each parses a tiny fixture into the unified `Message` link shape. (R-E1..E9, R-A1)\n4. **Patterns / replies / automation / CRM / facts** — simple regex inference, fuzzy reply ranker, dialog-graph data model, contact aggregator, set-algebra search, fact extractor. (R-B2/B3, R-C1..C5, R-D1..D4)\n5. **Sync seed** — last-writer-wins per-link CRDT merge + transport-agnostic peer interface ready for WebRTC. (R-F5)\n6. **Distribution** — `bin/meta-sovereign` CLI (lino-arguments-style), `serve` HTTP endpoint exposing storage, Electron main entry, two Dockerfiles, cargo workspace seed (`crates/meta-sovereign-core`) for the pure-Rust track. (R-F1..F7, R-G2/G3)\n7. **Quality** — TypeDoc config, expanded test suite (unit + integration), e2e harness placeholder against browser-commander's interface. (R-H3/H4)\n8. **Docs** — solution-plan.md updated with status per milestone; this PR's section in case study updated.\n\nWhat this PR is **not**: a finished React chat client at Telegram-Desktop quality, finished pattern-synthesis algorithms, finished n8n graph editor, finished WebRTC signalling, or a finished pure-Rust port. Those are explicitly the thickening work future PRs do on top of the skeletons landed here.\n\nIf you'd rather I instead pick one subsystem and ship it fully (e.g. just storage + Telegram import + CLI, end-to-end), say the word and I'll pivot.\n\nStarting now.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/issues/comments/4358648347/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/issues/comments/4358747054","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/pull/2#issuecomment-4358747054","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/meta-sovereign/issues/2","id":4358747054,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSRd4l88AAAABA80zrg","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-01T09:43:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-01T09:43:00Z","body":"## 🤖 Solution Draft Log\nThis log file contains the complete execution trace of the AI solution draft process.\n\n### 💰 Cost: **$6.257172**\n\n### 📊 **Context and tokens usage:**\n\n**Claude Opus 4.7:** (2 session segments)\n1. peak request: 44.9K / 1M (4%) input tokens, 46.0K / 128K (36%) output 