        "text": "The root cause: `startSyncListener.transport.send` immediately drops the event if no client is connected yet. This is a real bug, not just a flaky test. On bun-macOS, the Node.js server `connection` event fires after the client `'connect'` callback, opening this race window.\n\nI'll fix `tcp-transport.js` to expose a \"first connection ready\" promise so callers can wait, AND make the test wait for that. This is more robust than buffering writes (which has its own pitfalls):"
      }
    ],
