        "input": {
          "command": "git add .gitignore src/sync/tcp-transport.js && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nBuffer TCP sync events until first peer connects\n\nThe bun-on-macOS test runner intermittently failed sync-tcp because the\nserver's `connection` event can fire after the client's `connect`\ncallback resolves `connectSyncPeer`. The first event sent through\n`listener.transport.send` then iterated an empty `sockets` set and was\nsilently dropped, so replication never arrived and bun killed the test\nat its 5-second timeout.\n\nBuffer events while no peer is connected and flush them when the first\nsocket attaches. Fix is on the transport, not the test, so the same\nrace cannot bite real users either.\n\nAlso gitignore deno.lock — it's auto-generated when deno is invoked\nlocally and is not consumed by any CI step.\nEOF\n)\"",
